        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): MiniMax VLM can consume oversized success responses",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users invoking MiniMax VLM image understanding could have OpenClaw read an unbounded provider success response when MiniMax returns an unexpectedly large `200 OK` body. Non-OK MiniMax VLM responses already used a bounded diagnostic snippet, but successful JSON responses were not bounded before parsing.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMiniMax VLM successful responses are now read through the shared bounded response reader before JSON parsing, with a 256 KiB response-body cap and Trace-Id included in overflow errors. This keeps normal valid VLM results unchanged and does not change request payloads, provider routing, timeout behavior, or non-OK error snippet handling.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers and operators get bounded read behavior for malformed or oversized MiniMax VLM success responses. Normal MiniMax VLM image descriptions still return content as before; an oversized successful provider body now fails fast with a diagnostic error instead of being fully consumed.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRegression coverage now exercises an oversized successful MiniMax VLM JSON response and asserts that the response stream is cancelled before parsing the full body.\n\n- Public proof excerpt: Validation `minimax-vlm-test` (pass, exit_code=0, 13283ms):\n\n  ```text\n  [test] starting test/vitest/vitest.agents.config.ts\n  The `envFile` option is deprecated, please use `envDir: false` instead.\n\n   RUN  v4.1.9 [local path redacted]\n\n\n   Test Files  1 passed (1)\n        Tests  13 passed (13)\n     Start at  14:46:40\n     Duration  1.45s (transform 696ms, setup 494ms, import 279ms, tests 333ms, environment 0ms)\n\n  [test] passed 1 Vitest shard in 13.05s\n  ```\n",
        "branch": "fix/problem-minimax-vlm-success-byte-cap",
        "head_sha": "9f60c155cbac86c78fd6c216d9498c4e4b42020d",
